Sval: a profiler stopped by signal writes no file while private browsing is in use

SIGUSR2 stops a running profiler and writes its profile to the downloads
folder. A profile names the pages each process has open. While
SvalCrashPrivacy says a process could hold a private window's pages, the
signal stops the profiler and writes nothing.

diff --git a/tools/profiler/core/platform.cpp b/tools/profiler/core/platform.cpp
index 9839ed5751..7c199637fe 100644
--- a/tools/profiler/core/platform.cpp
+++ b/tools/profiler/core/platform.cpp
@@ -91,6 +91,7 @@
 #  include "mozilla/WindowsStackWalkInitialization.h"
 #endif
 #include "mozilla/StaticPtr.h"
+#include "mozilla/SvalCrashPrivacy.h"
 #include "mozilla/TimeStamp.h"
 #include "mozilla/UniquePtr.h"
 #include "mozilla/Vector.h"
@@ -5909,6 +5910,13 @@ void profiler_dump_and_stop() {
     return;
   }
 
+  // Sval: a profile names the pages each process has open, a private
+  // window's among them, so none is written while one could be in it.
+  if (mozilla::SvalCrashPrivacy::Get()) {
+    profiler_stop();
+    return;
+  }
+
   // pause the profiler until we are done dumping
   profiler_pause();
 
